<font size="+2">BLUNDER</font><br><br>
When the moon ascends<br>
to your skies and casts<br>
its light<br>
onto your sparkling stars<br><br>
When the sun swims<br>
in its journey over thee<br>
in that limitless and blue<br>
that mighty boundless sea<br><br>
When the stars<br>
sparkle green and sink<br>
into a reservoir of mercury<br>
and cast<br>
their shadows<br>
onto your heavens<br><br>
Your image is reflected<br>
in a mirror of silver,<br>
calming the soul<br>
alleviating the thunder<br>
streaking the lightening<br>
glistening the horizon<br><br>
astonishing Man whose<br>
heart is tender.<br><br>
My beloved land<br>
sometimes I wonder<br>
I thrive on how you<br>
shine in a mirror of silver<br><br>
And how you swim<br>
in an endless sea and<br>
a timeless space<br>
in a senseless vacuum<br>
an expanding universe<br><br>
Sometimes I wonder how<br>
you brighten the skies<br>
and this senseless world that<br>
ONLY KNOWS BLUNDER.<br>
</td>
</tr>
